# Cloudflare Pages configuration for redirects
# NOTE: the "!" forced-redirect suffix (301!) is NOT honoured on this
# deployment — verified in production: /home and /blog/post/:slug returned 404
# while every plain "301" rule resolved correctly. Plain 301 is safe here
# because no static file exists at these paths.
# /home -> / (redirect old React Router routes)
/home / 301

# Sitemap backward-compatibility redirect (Next.js -> Astro)
/sitemap.xml /sitemap-index.xml 301

# Legacy service worker cleanup redirect
/sw.js/ /sw.js 301

# Blog post redirects for old React Router structure
/blog/post/:slug /blog/:slug/ 301

# Evergreen blog slugs: the "-2024" suffix aged badly in the SERP now that the
# content is genuinely current (1405 refresh). These three URLs are already
# live and indexed, so they MUST keep resolving. Both slash variants are listed
# because the legacy Next.js build served them with a trailing slash.
/blog/seo-guide-2024 /blog/seo-guide/ 301
/blog/seo-guide-2024/ /blog/seo-guide/ 301
/blog/google-ads-guide-2024 /blog/google-ads-guide/ 301
/blog/google-ads-guide-2024/ /blog/google-ads-guide/ 301
/blog/digital-marketing-trends-2024 /blog/digital-marketing-trends/ 301
/blog/digital-marketing-trends-2024/ /blog/digital-marketing-trends/ 301

# API redirects (if any)
